Collect per-queue metrics using IBM PCF wildcard (generic) queue names: the check now issues one `INQUIRE_Q` / `INQUIRE_Q_STATUS` / `RESET_Q_STATS` command per queue manager instead of two or three per queue. This takes the per-queue PCF command count from roughly 3N to 3, reducing both the check's CPU and the load placed on the queue manager's command server, which previously scaled with the number of monitored queues. Emitted metrics are unchanged, and collection falls back to per-queue commands when a bulk response is unavailable.
